Hi,

just some minor comments:

>  cdfEnsb<-AffymetrixCdfFile$fromChipType(paste(chipType,"U-Ensembl47,G-Affy",sep=","))

This is more naturally done as (and slightly less error prone):

cdfEnsb <- AffymetrixCdfFile$fromChipType(chipType, tags="U-Ensembl47,G-Affy")

>  > In spite of the exceptions thrown, fit(plm, ...) appears to run to
>  > completion, and the script writes expression data (?) to file:

I guess you refer to the fact that the output ends as:

>  >  Identifying non-estimated units...done
>  > Fitting model of class ExonRmaPlm:...done

Unfortunately this only means that all "opened" verbose statements
stacked internally are "closed".  Ideally, all "...done" should be
replaced by "...error" if an error occurs, but the framework for
reporting that is not in place.

/Henrik

