This is not correct (=wrong).  Rule #1 when using aroma.affymetrix is
that you should never ever have to specify an absolute pathname, e.g.
"~/annotationData/...".  If you have code that does that, that is a
strong indication you're on the wrong trail.  Instead, use the
AffymetrixCdfFile$fromChipType() construct.  See examples online.

> > print(cdf)
> AffymetrixCdfFile:
> Path: /Users/jeremiah/annotationData/chipType/DogSty06m520431
> Filename: DogSty06m520431.cdf
> Filesize: 84.63MB
>
> File format: v4 (binary; XDA)
> Chip type: DogSty06m520431
> Dimension: 1612x1612
> Number of cells: 2598544
> Number of units: 127201
> Cells per unit: 20.43
>
> Number of QC units: 0
> RAM: 0.00MB
> > cs <- AffymetrixCelSet$Fromfiles("~/annotationData/rawData/", cdf=cdf)
> Error: attempt to apply non-function
> > cs <- AffymetrixCelSet$fromFiles("~/annotationData/rawData/", cdf=cdf)

Also incorrect. Use the AffymetrixCelSet$fromName() construct.  See
examples online and follow Suggestion (2) above.

Cheers

