are you aware that you can setup R to connection to internet via a
proxy?  Basically, if you can surf the web via a proxy, you can have R
do the same.  I haven't had to do this myself so I don't know the
details, but I've seen it discussed over the years and it seem like
people get it to work.  See the R help and ask for more help at the
r-help list.

